    "updated_at": "2020-03-11T16:44:13Z",
    "body": "> I was thinking to update the documentation but I was wondering why is it disabled by default ?\r\n\r\nJust to clarify, this is the module's default configuration:\r\n```toml\r\n[git_commit]\r\ncommit_hash_length = 7\r\nprefix = \"(\"\r\nsuffix = \") \"\r\nstyle = \"bold green\"\r\nonly_detached = true\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe intended behavior is to only show the commit hash in the detached-head state. To most developers, the commit hash is not actionable information, unless they're not at the head of a branch.\r\n\r\nI'm open to discussing alternative default behavior, but as it is, I think it serves the needs of most developers.",
